## 2. COMPONENT SPECIFICATIONS

**2.1 Buttons** — Flex layout (`display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 0.5rem`), min touch target 44×44px. States via classes: hover (lift + `--shadow-md`), focus-visible (2px `--color-primary` outline, 2px offset), active (`transform: translateY(0)` / scale feedback), loading (spinner or animated Google Icon, dimensions preserved, double-click prevented), disabled (`opacity: .5`, greyscale, `cursor: not-allowed`), and success/error feedback using `--text-success` / `--text-error`. `.btn--primary` uses the dark `--color-primary` fill with light `#f2ead9` text; `.btn-danger` (if any footer/destructive link needs it) must be visually distinct in both themes.

**2.2 Cards** — `.card` base: `--color-surface` + `var(--hatch-fine)` background, `var(--border-certificate)` double-rule border, `--shadow-md`, `--radius-lg`, `--space-6` padding. Interactive cards (pricing tiers, feature cards): hover `translateY(-2px)` with `--shadow-lg`; `:focus-within` highlights the border in `--color-primary`; skeleton shimmer state defined in CSS; empty-state fallback with a Google Icon and guidance text where content is dynamic.

**2.3 Forms & Inputs** — `.input` per the token spec (hatched `--color-surface-strong` background, 1.5px ink border, focus ring `0 0 0 3px rgba(90,46,18,0.25)`). Wrap as flex containers: label, input, dedicated error container. Cover states: empty, focused, filled, valid (success border + Google check icon), invalid (error border, error text, icon), disabled, read-only. Use in the Final CTA email capture and FAQ search if included.

**2.4 FAQ Accordion / Modals** — If FAQ uses `<details>`/`<summary>` or a custom accordion: full keyboard operability, ARIA (`aria-expanded`, `aria-controls`), animated open/close via CSS transitions, focus-visible styling. Any modal: centered flex container, backdrop overlay, Google Icon close button, focus trapping, `Esc` and overlay-click close, opening/open/closing animations.

