## 3. CORE UX & MICRO-INTERACTION RULES

- **Signature texture:** apply `var(--hatch-fine)` cross-hatch under every surface (body, nav, cards, inputs) and the certificate double-rule border on nav, cards, and inputs — the page must read as an engraved plate, not flat print. Add engraved-style section dividers (double rules / ornamental rule lines) between sections.
- **Hero:** large `--font-display` headline in `--color-ink`, monospace eyebrow label, primary + secondary CTA buttons. Simulate engraved illustration with layered CSS hatching (repeating-linear-gradient at multiple angles/densities) — no images required, but any decorative texture must be pure CSS.
- **Pricing:** 3 tiers, middle tier visually elevated (surface-strong + `--shadow-lg` + badge "Most Popular" using `.badge`).
- **Testimonials:** quote cards with monospace attribution, engraved quotation ornament.
- **Responsive by default**, no horizontal overflow. Smooth transitions (`var(--transition-normal)`) on all state changes, honoring `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **Accessibility:** sufficient contrast in both light and dark modes; never rely on color alone for state; semantic HTML5 (`header`, `main`, `section`, `footer`, `nav`); logical focus order; `aria-live` regions for dynamic feedback (form errors, toasts, loading).
- **Mandatory visual feedback** on every click/hover/submission. All user-facing copy in **English**, written to fit the premium heritage/engraving brand voice (no lorem ipsum).

---

## 4. DELIVERABLES

- **Files:** separate `index.html`, `style.css`, `script.js`. Only a single deferred `<script src="script.js" defer>` reference in the HTML — no inline script blocks.
- **Naming:** one consistent BEM-style convention (`.btn`, `.btn--primary`, `.card`, `.nav__link`, `.pricing__tier`) throughout.
- **script.js scope:** theme toggle + persistence, FAQ accordion behavior, form validation feedback, and button loading-state simulation only. No frameworks, no build steps.
- Validate both light and dark modes before declaring completion.
